          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            One incarnation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic principle
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            is the correspondence between 3d
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk+field+theory"} bulk field theory
            and the 2d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wess-Zumino-Witten+model"} Wess-Zumino-Witten model
            on a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            as the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic principle
            was formulated as such, motivated from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk+field+theories"} bulk field theories
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theorem"} theorem
            instead of just a vague
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjecture"} conjecture
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
          %p
            Indeed, the natural equivalence between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surface"} surface
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            and the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            was understood in the seminal article (
            %a{:href => "#Witten89"}> Witten 89
            ) and subsequently discussed in much detail, see also at
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Chern-Simons%20theory#References"} CS-theory – References
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavefunctions"} wavefunctions
            of Chern-Simons theory and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlators"} correlators
            of the WZW model is reviewed for instance in (
            %a{:href => "#Gawedzki99"}> Gawędzki 99, around p. 30
            ). For the case of abelian gauge group and with an eye towards generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-dual higher gauge theory
            a review is in (
            %a{:href => "#Witten96"}> Witten 96, section 2
            ). (This correspondence is captured
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functorially
            by the notion of the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+functor"} modular functor
            of the 2d theory, see there for more.)
          %p
            For instance the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FRS+formalism"} FRS formalism
            %em constructs
            all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+conformal+field+theories"} rational conformal field theories
            as full
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FQFTs"} FQFTs
            holographically from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reshetikhin-Turaev+construction"} Reshetikhin-Turaev construction
            of the 3d Chern-Simons theory and fully classifies them this way.
          %p
            Later the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
            came to be understood as a canonical or default implementation of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic principle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk+field+theory"} bulk field theory
            is a theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d+quantum+gravity"} 3d quantum gravity
            which is very much like traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            but may crucially differ from it, see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+gravity"} Chern-Simons gravity
            the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Chern-Simons%20gravity#ProblemsInTheNonPerturbativeRegime"} comments on the non-perturbative regime
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#GukovMartinecMooreStrominger04"} Gukov-Martinec-Moore-Strominger 04
          %p
            But notice that also plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+strings"} topological strings
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TCFT"} TCFT
            the section
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "TCFT#ActionFunctionals"} Worldsheet and effective background theories
          %p
            A general argument that in sectors of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            on the CFT-side are given just by the
            = succeed "-sector" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} higher dimensional Chern-Simons theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            theory is in (
            %a{:href => "#Witten98"}> Witten98
            ). This applies notably to the duality between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} 7-dimensional Chern-Simons theory
            and the conformal blocks in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
            on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
