            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+1-brane+in+3d"} super 1-brane in 3d
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TT+deformation"} TT deformation
          %h2#references References
          %h3#cswzw CS/WZW
          %p The original article on the CS/WZW correspondence is
          %ul
            %li#Witten89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum Field Theory and the Jones Polynomial
              %strong 121
              3 (1989) 351399 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104178138"}> euclid:.cmp/1104178138
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01217730"} doi:10.1007/BF01217730
          %p More details worked out:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+C.+Cabra"}> Daniel C. Cabra
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gerardo+L.+Rossini"} Gerardo L. Rossini
              = succeed "," do
                %em Explicit connection between conformal field theory and 2+1 Chern-Simons theory
              %strong 12
              (1997) 1687-1697 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9506054"}> arXiv:hep-th/9506054
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217732397001722"} doi:10.1142/S0217732397001722
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (with motivation from
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laughlin+wavefunctions"} Laughlin wavefunctions
                  for
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anyons"} anyons
                  in
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+matter+theory"} condensed matter theory
          %p Reviews:
          %ul
            %li#Gawedzki99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Krzysztof+Gaw%C4%99dzki"}> Krzysztof Gawędzki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conformal field theory: a case study
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conformal Field Theory – New Non-perturbative Methods In String And Field Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9904145"} arXiv:hep-th/9904145
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1201/9780429502873"} doi:10.1201/9780429502873
            %li#Witten96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                , section 2 of:
                %em Five-Brane Effective Action In M-Theory
                J. Geom. Phys.
                %strong 22
                (1997) 103-133 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9610234"}> arXiv:hep-th/9610234
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Tran Quang Loc:
                %em Wess-Zumino-Witten models and their correspondence to Chern-Simons theories
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/quangloctran/quangloctran.github.io/blob/master/essay.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://indico.in2p3.fr/event/19437/contributions/89681/attachments/61365/83940/vsop26_TranQuangLoc.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Loc-WZWCS.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The relation of this
            = succeed "-duality" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi CS
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi WZW
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CS_3/WZW_2
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
          %ul
            %li#GukovMartinecMooreStrominger04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+Gukov"}> Sergei Gukov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emil+Martinec"} Emil Martinec
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"} Gregory Moore
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Strominger"} Andrew Strominger
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Chern-Simons Gauge Theory and the
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi AdS
                            %mn 3
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi CFT
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_3/CFT_2
                    Correspondence
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Shifman"} Mikhail Shifman
                et al. (eds.)
                = succeed "," do
                  %em From fields to strings
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0403225"} arXiv:hep-th/0403225
            %li
              %p
                Kristan Jensen,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Chiral anomalies and AdS/CMT in two dimensions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1012.4831"} arXiv:1012.4831
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Kraus"}> Per Kraus
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Finn+Larsen"} Finn Larsen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Partition functions and elliptic genera from supergravity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0607138"} arXiv:hep-th/0607138
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Kraus"}> Per Kraus
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Lectures on black holes and the
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi AdS
                            %mn 3
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msub
                            %mi CFT
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AdS_3/CFT_2
                    correspondence
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0609074"} arXiv:hep-th/0609074
            %li
              %p
                Ville Keranen,
                %em Chern-Simons interactions in AdS3 and the current conformal block
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1403.6881"}> arXiv:1403.6881
                )
          %p
            A general argument about the relation between AdS/CFT duality and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/infinity-Chern-Simons+theory"} infinity-Chern-Simons theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Witten98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
